  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the continuation of the famous Marinières beach, this small, somewhat hidden pebble cove offers a picturesque setting with views over the Villefranche bay. It's the only stretch of beach in the area where dogs are allowed, on the left as you face the sea.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is via the Marinière car park (right at the end) or via Boulevard Napoléon III then Avenue de l'Ange Gardien. Parking can be tricky right by the beach — better to use the paid car park and walk a little.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the pebble slope is gentle, handy if your dog is just learning to swim — but watch for fatigue, as salt and effort tire them out fast.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Villefranche, with its picturesque harbour and the Saint-Pierre chapel decorated by Cocteau, is worth a stroll after the swim. Several terraces in the area welcome dogs.</p>
    </div>

